  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =\\overset{\u00af}{x}+0.8\\cdot \\sigma .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}37 & =\\overset{\u00af}{x}+1.2\\cdot \\sigma .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(37-28) & =(1.2-0.8)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 9 & =0.4\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =22.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
